## Types

```mdl
type Recording
  desc: >
    The takes recorded for a presentation (typename org.dxos.type.recording), parented to it. Each take is a
    Variant of one of its owned MediaArtifacts, by kind.
  fields:
    name?: string
    presentation: Ref<Presentation>
    audio?: Ref<MediaArtifact>        # kind 'audio': voice-only takes
    video?: Ref<MediaArtifact>        # kind 'video': takes with a screen or camera picture
```

```mdl
type Take.Log
  desc: >
    A take's timeline, held in its Variant's `config`. Times are seconds on the take's own clock; a section is one
    visit to a slide.
  fields:
    sections: { id, title?, start, end }[]   # id is the Slide's id
    steps: { id, step, at }[]                # click steps revealed
    duration: number
    device?: string                          # microphone label
    source: none | screen | camera
```

```mdl
type RecorderSettings
  fields:
    audioInput?: string               # microphone deviceId; unset prefers a /shure/i device, else the first
    videoSource?: none | screen | camera
    videoInput?: string               # camera deviceId
```

## Components

```mdl
component RecordButton
  desc: >
    The presenter toolbar item (PresenterSurface.Toolbar). Inside its click it creates the AudioContext, opens the
    microphone (processing off) and the screen or camera when set, starts the take, then presents the deck from its
    first slide. It is disabled while a take starts, records or saves, and shows why the last start failed.
  props: { subject: Presentation }

component RecordingOverlay
  desc: >
    Over a deck being recorded (PresenterSurface.Overlay), centered at the top: REC, the take's length, the time left
    on the slide when it has a desired length (red once over), and a compact level meter that shows a readout only to
    warn (NO SIGNAL, CLIP).
  props: { subject: Presentation }

component LevelMeter
  desc: >
    Peak meter over -60..0 dBFS: the target band -12..-3 marked, a peak-hold marker for 1.5s, CLIP above -1 dBFS,
    and NO SIGNAL after 2s of digital silence.
  props: { peakDb?, holdDb?, rmsDb?, silent?, clip?, compact? }

component RecordingsArticle
  desc: >
    The Recordings companion of a Presentation. Its toolbar has Record (as the presentation's own item). It lists
    unsaved takes (with Save again, Download, Discard), then each saved take, newest first, with Play (an inline
    player), Download and Delete, and each slide's recorded length against the slide's desired length, flagged when
    over.
  props: { presentation: Presentation }

component RecorderSettings
  desc: The plugin settings: microphone and camera pickers, the video source, and Test microphone with the meter.
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Record a voice-over
  req F-1.1: A Presentation's toolbar has a Record item; pressing it starts a take and presents the deck from its first slide.
  req F-1.2: The microphone is opened with echo cancellation, noise suppression and auto gain off.
  req F-1.3: Each slide change and click step while presenting is logged in the take's timeline.
  req F-1.4: Leaving the presentation ends the take and saves it as a new Variant, named by its start time; no take is overwritten.
  req F-1.5: A take that cannot be saved stays listed with Save again, Save as a file and Discard.
  req F-1.6: While recording, the presented deck shows REC, the take's length and a level meter with NO SIGNAL and CLIP warnings, but no level readout.
  req F-1.7: While recording a slide with a desired length, the overlay shows the time left on it, and how far over once it runs past.

feat F-2: Takes
  req F-2.1: A Presentation has a Recordings companion listing its takes, newest first, each with a player.
  req F-2.2: Each take lists every slide it showed with its recorded length and the slide's desired length; a slide over its desired length is flagged.
  req F-2.3: The latest take of each kind is its artifact's cover.
  req F-2.4: The companion's toolbar starts a take, as the presentation's Record item does.
  req F-2.5: Each saved take can be played in place, downloaded as a file, and deleted; deleting the cover makes the newest remaining take the cover.

feat F-3: Settings
  req F-3.1: The settings choose the microphone, the video source (none, screen, camera) and the camera.
  req F-3.2: Test microphone opens the chosen microphone on the level meter without recording.
  req F-3.3: With no microphone chosen, a device whose label matches /shure/i is preferred.
```

## QA

```mdl
test QA-1: Record a voice-over of a presentation
  desc: The primary journey — record a take while presenting a deck, then find it in the Recordings companion.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-1.1, F-1.3, F-1.4, F-1.6, F-2.1, F-2.2]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - a Presentation named "QA Recording" with two slides, each with speaker notes; the first slide's Duration is 5
    - Recorder settings: video source None; a working microphone
    - the presenter's Speaker notes setting is Subtitles
  steps:
    - name: Start the take
      do: Open "QA Recording" and press Record in its toolbar; allow the microphone.
      expect: the deck presents from slide 1, REC and a moving level meter show top-left, and slide 1's notes show as subtitles
      note: NO `invoke` — the take must start inside a click (the media prompt and the AudioContext need it).
    - name: Read and advance
      do: Read the first slide's notes for more than 5 seconds, press →, read the second slide's notes.
      expect: the subtitles change to slide 2's notes
    - name: End the take
      do: Press Escape.
      expect: the presentation closes; REC is gone
    - name: Find the take
      do: Open the presentation's Recordings companion.
      expect: one take, named take-<date>-<time>, with a player; slide 1's recorded length is flagged over its 0:05
  after:
    - name: Delete the recording
      do: Delete the "QA Recording" presentation (its Recording is parented to it).
      expect: the presentation and its takes are gone
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: A new plugin records a presentation's voice-over from a script, working with plugin-studio; a take is stored as a studio MediaArtifact.
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Recording]
```

```mdl
decision D-2: The plugin is named plugin-recorder; post-processing (trim, stretch, mux, loudness) runs on native ffmpeg, as an EDGE compute operation and as a desktop sidecar; video is a screen capture with a camera overlay, leaving room for other picture sources (autocue videos, canvas animations, presenter decks); plugin-presenter is the harness for the script.
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Recording, F-1]
```

```mdl
decision D-3: plugin-recorder adds a toolbar item to the presenter that starts the presentation and records its voice-over, and has settings to choose the microphone and the video source and to test the microphone.
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [RecordButton, RecorderSettings, F-1.1, F-3]
```

```mdl
decision D-4: A Recording is parented to its Presentation and owns one MediaArtifact per kind (audio, video); each take is a Variant with its timeline in `config`, so no take type of its own exists. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Recording, Take.Log]
  why: Studio's Variant is already "one produced alternative with the request that made it"; a take is exactly that.
  rejected: A Take ECHO type beside Variant, which would duplicate studio's media model.
```

```mdl
decision D-5: A take's timeline is on the take's own clock, one section per slide visit keyed by Slide id, with click steps logged apart; recording starts with the presentation, with no hold before the first slide. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Take.Log, F-1.3]
  why: A deck has no picture timeline of its own, and ids survive slide reorders where positions do not.
```

```mdl
decision D-6: The recorder is a capability service rather than state in the toolbar item, and follows the presentation through presenter's PresentationEventHandler. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [RecordButton, F-1.3, F-1.4]
  why: The toolbar unmounts while the deck is presented; presenter must not depend on the recorder.
```

```mdl
decision D-7: A take that fails to save stays in memory with Save again and Save as a file; buffering it to IndexedDB is deferred. Takes are listed in a Recordings companion of the Presentation, not as navtree objects. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [RecordingsArticle, F-1.5, F-2.1]
  why: A take is the one thing the workflow must never lose; a companion keeps takes beside the deck they voice.
```

```mdl
decision D-8: Phase 1 records one video source (screen or camera); the camera overlay on a screen capture, post-processing, and other picture sources are later phases. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-1, RecorderSettings]
  why: Compositing the overlay needs a canvas pipeline; post-processing needs the EDGE and desktop runners.
```

```mdl
decision D-9: The Recordings companion has a toolbar, and each recording can be played, downloaded and deleted.
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [RecordingsArticle, F-2.4, F-2.5]
```

```mdl
decision D-10: The recording panel and its meter are centered horizontally over the deck and show the time remaining on the slide when it has a desired length; the peak and level readout is not shown while recording.
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [RecordingOverlay, LevelMeter, F-1.6, F-1.7]
```

```mdl
decision D-11: The overlay's compact meter still shows NO SIGNAL and CLIP, as warnings only; the companion plays a take with its own player rather than studio's VariantRenderer surface. Fills in [D-9] and [D-10].
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [LevelMeter, RecordingsArticle]
  why: A muted microphone silently ruined two takes in the prototype; studio's surface renders only while plugin-studio is enabled.
```
